      "body": "Captions flicker because most engines rewrite the last line every time a new hypothesis arrives. Fixing that needs a rendering contract, not a better model. We lock finalized segments in place and only append.\n\nThe result is fewer regressive eye movements and a transcript people can actually read while speaking. This paragraph exists so the thread splitter has enough text to produce more than one tweet."
